{
 "state": "WV",
 "file": "WV Social Studies Stadards.docx",
 "structure": "West Virginia College- and Career-Readiness Standards for Social Studies (Policy 2520.4, Title 126 Series 44D), Word document. Front matter (u1-u54): legislative rule sections 1-5, Introduction, Explanation of Terms and numbering (SS.<grade or course>.<number>, e.g. SS.3.1, SS.W.20), four content-area descriptions (Civics, Economics, Geography, History), indicators intro and literacy note. Then grade-band indicator charts (K-2 u55-u66, 3-5 u220-u231, 6-8 u393-u404, 9-12 u571-u582): two-column table with a Develop-questions row, then Civics/Economics, Geography/History(+Literacy) header rows each followed by a single cell of paragraph-form indicators; these are standards for that band. K-8: each grade has a 'Grade Standards' heading, an overview paragraph (examples), then one table per strand (Civics, Economics, Geography, History, WV History) whose first row is the strand title and each following row is [code SS.g.n | standard text]; K=SS.K.1-22, 1=SS.1.1-23, 2=SS.2.1-21, 3=SS.3.1-23, 4=SS.4.1-19, 5=SS.5.1-28, 6=SS.6.1-24, 7=SS.7.1-24, 8=SS.8.1-26 (8th grade is West Virginia Studies, grade-level, not a course). Grades 9-12: indicator chart, then one section per course with a title, overview paragraph (examples) and strand tables with coded rows: World Studies SS.W.1-28, United States Studies SS.US.1-23 (described as Tenth Grade, so grade 10), United States Studies - Comprehensive SS.USC.1-30, Contemporary Studies SS.CS.1-24, Civics SS.C.1-37 (plus a Personal Finance embedding note), Economics SS.E.1-43, Geography SS.G.1-25, Sociology SS.S.1-35, Psychology SS.P.1-27 (domain headers Scientific Inquiry, Biopsychology, Cognition, etc., and Application rows for careers). Appendix A: Personal Finance standards numbered 1-10 (no SS prefix) to be embedded in Civics. Examples/e.g. lists are inside the standard text (not labeled separately). Table cells are [T n R r C c]; C1 is code or strand title, C2 is text.",
